{% doc %}
  user_login hook (pos-module-user, fired after every password sign-in on the
  instance). While an email is locked after 5 failed desk sign-ins, a sign-in
  through another form (the host's /sessions) is undone, so the lock cannot
  be bypassed there. Failed attempts on other forms are not seen by the desk:
  the host rate-limits its own sign-in form (README, Security).
  @param {object} params - { user, hook_params }
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  function locked = 'modules/support/queries/sign_in/locked', email: params.user.email
  if locked
    graphql _ = 'modules/user/session/destroy'
    log params.user.id, type: 'support_sign_in_locked'
    return { "support_sign_in_locked": true }
  endif
  return null
%}
